.1/chat.md","size_bytes":4032},"commits":{"digest":"165ccf2724b77aacd333a7d0271cf8383e8fb25443671cc0ff229bfd7572cab6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1/commits.json","size_bytes":250},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"901c66c468693b9a10115c8b9f5876c071df6dd6116e1776a29ebeed460e18c5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1/meta.json","size_bytes":5341},"prompt":{"digest":"12a6b79b18eabd0ad8c969a210bf585852e38c30032d0e40e176292663bd4d1e","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":173},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"5e33168ca514640ba4365106a0e411a69d44080dbacaa73f6967caabfdb98ff5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":8084},"state":{"digest":"62a631924119e3aad6e9efbc7eb9af2068ca9ebb5c64f0ab88b25c99e4451282","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-09-22T18:03:03.609980+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-16h.1","local_name":"sase-16h.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-16h","agent_clan_generation":"20260922130659","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-16h.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-16h[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]E1.5: enforced sase tool adoption and monitor wrapping[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every heavy verification run by a SASE agent is a recorded ToolRun [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]by construction: guarded recipes refuse a raw agent invocation, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]monitors wrap what they run, the wrapper is at least as faithful as[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the raw command, and the linked repos carry their own catalogs and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]guards.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]tool_e15_enforced_adoption.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make an agent an ownership root and always export the wrapper [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]marker[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]ownership-roots[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ownership-roots: scrub executor-ownership variables at every agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch, ignore an inherited monitor/proc id under SASE_AGENT, always [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]export SASE_TOOL_NAME and SASE_TOOL_PROJECT_ROOT, and carry a monitor's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]starter agent into its recorded runs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Record child process facts and authorize reaping in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-child-facts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ownership-roots[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-child-facts: add the sase-core wire, store write, and binding that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]persist a running run's child pid, pgid, and process identity, extend [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconcile to return identity-matched reap candidates, and move sase's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]core revision pin past that commit.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the wrapper as faithful as the raw command[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]wrapper-fidelity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-child-facts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wrapper-fidelity: keep the child in the wrapper's process group under a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live owner, make an inline child die with its wrapper, reap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity-matched survivors of lost runs, and give the child one merged [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pipe whenever a single target receives both streams.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Refuse a raw agent invocation of a guarded recipe[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]recipe-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wrapper-fidelity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]recipe-guard: add the dependency-free tools/require_tool_run script, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire it into check and check-full, document the environment contract, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]teach the adoption report bypasses and refusals, and record the decision[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that partly supersedes record-before-admit.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wrap a monitor's command in sase tool run[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]monitor-wrap[dim] · [dim][/dim]after recipe-guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor-wrap: upgrade an exact catalog match to a named run and wrap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]other verify-profile commands ad-hoc, in the proc argv only, behind a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor.tool_wrap config field, leaving monitor_command and host [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]completion bindings untouched.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Give the linked repos catalogs and guards[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]linked-repo-catalogs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after monitor-wrap[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]linked-repo-catalogs: add project tools catalogs and the recipe guard to[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core, sase-telegram, sase-github, and sase-research-artifacts so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enforcement and named upgrades reach the raw residual that lives outside[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase repo.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe"